    "difficulty": "easy",
    "dimension": "logicalCorrectness",
    "explanation": "Disjunctive (either-or) statements should be treated as a single statement because they express one complete thought—that one of two alternatives is true. The arguer is not asserting either alternative individually, only the disjunction as a whole.",
